{"title":"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark_on_Above_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark on Above Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there are infinitely many natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with the following property: the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3744d2b20b3e44f8d1204739ebdca4464cf411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = n^4 + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> is not prime for any natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e18948462f391408552d731433400f18adb631d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4k^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies the property outlined above.\n</p><p>The polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e098066e2631f0b80dd927113d52c3a343f1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4 + 4k^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> can be factored as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/72361522cb7d2c5daa5ae75eb77f74dbfdcece7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^4 + 4k^4\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/357daa0e2be5a29f749aed9641348e55c19b9dd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= n^4 + 4n^2k^2 + 4k^4 - 4n^2k^2\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f43938370e83a32d5f64fa354b0313538bd146f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (n^2 + 2k^2)^2 - (2nk)^2\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44cc5332167252a24cfbe3fdb6fe6c68ba95ac2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (n^2 + 2k^2 - 2nk)(n^2 + 2k^2 + 2nk)\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Both factors are positive, because if the left one is negative, then the right one would also negative, which is clearly false.\n</p><p>It is also simple to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07dac354fe05f0fcb4f2ab08807d5b844d30e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 + 2k^2 - 2nk &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c0b0da0238fca3dbfa04034c95d25b5ccfbfbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> is a valid value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, completing the proof. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark_on_Above_Solution\">Remark on Above Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark on Above Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The factorization <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336ab2c35a12b2670b343f979bd4d32128914f68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^4+4k^4=(n^2+2k^2-2nk)(n^2+2k^2+2nk)\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" />is a well-known result known as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sophie_Germain_Identity\" title=\"Sophie Germain Identity\">Sophie Germain Identity</a>. Also, for the sake of completing the proof of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43723a2f59d9b6ce0fb71246b94803afe91f09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+2k^2-2nk&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ff8ea020546fb6e8c90abbfb0b50802eee802d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b994f6cf36022c40e16511dd466ef6ce5548a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2+2k^2-2nk&gt;n^2+2-2n=(n-1)^2+1\\ge0+1=1.\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"20\" />Thus, we have the proof closed.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO\" title=\"1969 IMO\">1969 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170114\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 134/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1212/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3747/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.882      1 -total\n 53.89%    6.403      1 Template:IMO_box\n 45.07%    5.355      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9014:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170114 and revision id 284495. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}